# E2E tests (Cypress + Playwright live UI)

Browser UI against the **live API**—**not** HTTP API suites (`api-tests`), **not** mock UI (`mock-ui-tests`), and **not** Appium (`ios-e2e-tests` / `android-e2e-tests`).

- Prefer the `e2e-test-author` skill. Write **both** Cypress and Playwright unless the user names one framework.
- Specs: `cypress/tests/e2e/*.cy.ts`, `playwright/e2e/*.spec.ts` or top-level `playwright/*.spec.ts` until moved under `e2e/`. Mock UI specs live under `e2e/mock-ui/` and use `mock-ui-test-author`.
- Page objects required: `cypress/pages/`, `playwright/pages/`—no raw `data-testid` strings scattered in specs. Prefer the `page-object-author` skill when adding or extending POs.
- Selectors: `data-testid` via `cy.get("[data-testid=…]")` / `page.getByTestId(…)`.
- Auth: `loginAsCustomer` / `loginAsAdmin` from each framework’s `support/login.ts`, then navigate with the page object.
- Assert visible UI and URL/path—not response JSON schemas (those belong in `api-tests`).
- Keep Cypress and Playwright flows aligned on the same user journey.
